  "method_note": "Population exposure is estimated by projecting WorldPop 100 m (3 arc-sec, 2020, UN-adjusted) grid cell centers onto the 80 m NISAR UTM grid (EPSG:32611) and summing population where cumulative 108-day LOS subsidence is <= -2.0 cm (> 2 cm sinking) and <= -5.0 cm (> 5 cm sinking). Both strictly valid InSAR pixels and a <= 2.5 km nearest-neighbor basin interpolation (covering vegetated rural parcels) are reported. Crop exposure samples the 30 m USDA NASS Cropland Data Layer (CDL 2021) across the 80 m NISAR common-valid-pixel grid (0.0064 km^2/pixel)."
